  "question": {
    "text": "Dehydration of the following in increasing order is <br/>(I) <img src=\"assets\\qt0048_29e13cbaabb6.png\" style=\"width:1.05347in;height:0.61319in\"> <br/>(II) <img src=\"assets\\qt0048_3161ba0c3eaa.png\" style=\"width:1.12708in;height:0.65347in\"> <br/>(III) <img src=\"assets\\qt0048_1822f2e8c018.png\" style=\"width:1.2in;height:0.66667in\"> <br/>(IV) <img src=\"assets\\qt0048_83e7e9844d65.png\" style=\"width:1.13333in;height:0.64653in\">"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "I &lt; II &lt; III &lt; IV",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "II &lt; III &lt; IV &lt; I",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "I &lt; III &lt; IV &lt; II",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "None of these",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Dehydration of IV is most facile since, it gives an aromatic compound. Dehydration of III gives a conjugated diene which is stabilized by resonance. <br/><img src=\"assets\\st0048_309ee4f6a01b.png\" style=\"width:2.3in;height:0.74653in\"> <br/><img src=\"assets\\st0048_8f7ab3dbdb6a.png\" style=\"width:2.27986in;height:0.75972in\"> <br/>Dehydration of II gives only cyclohexene which is not stabilized by resonance. <br/><img src=\"assets\\st0048_2ee8ce04a1bf.png\" style=\"width:2.25347in;height:0.75347in\"> <br/>In contrast, phenol (I) does not undergo dehydration. Thus, the ease of dehydration is <br/>IV &gt; III &gt; II &gt; I."
  }
}